{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XoL4vEuT2BgCLKGLyPudV3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd081-basenc\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/basenc: Encode and Decode with Multiple Alphabets\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  GNU basenc is a generalized encoding utility that supports multiple encoding schemes\n6\t  beyond base32 and base64. macOS does not ship basenc. The Go implementation must match\n7\t  the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gbasenc, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n8\t  all flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Encode or decode data using a selectable encoding scheme.\n12\t  - G2: Support Base64, Base64URL, Base32, Base32hex, Base16, and Z85 encodings.\n13\t  - G3: Support line wrapping and garbage ignoring like base32/base64.\n14\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gbasenc via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Encoding schemes\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: \"--base64 must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base64 (same as base64 utility).\"\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"--base64url must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base64 with URL-safe alphabet (+ and / replaced by - and _).\"\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: \"--base32 must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base32 (same as base32 utility).\"\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: \"--base32hex must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base32 with extended hex alphabet.\"\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Additional encodings and options\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"--base16 must encode/decode using hexadecimal (Base16). Output is uppercase hex characters.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: \"--z85 must encode/decode using ZeroMQ Z85 encoding. Input length must be a multiple of 4 bytes for encoding.\"\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: \"-d or --decode must decode the input using the selected encoding scheme.\"\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: \"-w COLS or --wrap=COLS must set the wrap column (default 76). -w 0 disables wrapping.\"\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Input handling and error cases\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: \"-i or --ignore-garbage must ignore non-alphabet characters during decoding.\"\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given).\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: Must exit 1 when no encoding scheme is specified, when the file cannot be opened, or when decode input is invalid.\n50\t      - R3.4:\n51\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n52\t\n53\tnon_goals:\n54\t  - cmd/basenc does not implement Base2 (binary) encoding.\n55\t  - cmd/basenc does not implement custom alphabet specification.\n56\t\n57\tpackage_contract:\n58\t  imports:\n59\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\n60\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n61\t\n62\tacceptance_criteria:\n63\t  - id: AC1\n64\t    criterion: \"echo hello | basenc --base64 produces Base64 encoded output matching gbasenc --base64.\"\n65\t    traces:\n66\t      - R1.1\n67\t      - R2.4\n68\t  - id: AC2\n69\t    criterion: \"echo hello | basenc --base16 produces hex output matching gbasenc --base16.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R2.1\n72\t  - id: AC3\n73\t    criterion: \"basenc --base64url encodes with URL-safe alphabet, matching gbasenc --base64url.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.2\n76\t  - id: AC4\n77\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gbasenc passes for all required test cases.\"\n78\t    traces:\n79\t      - R1.1\n80\t      - R1.2\n81\t      - R1.3\n82\t      - R1.4\n83\t      - R2.1\n84\t      - R2.2\n85\t      - R2.3\n86\t  - id: AC5\n87\t    criterion: \"cmd/basenc compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n88\t    traces:\n89\t      - R1.1\n90\t      - R1.2\n91\t      - R1.3\n92\t      - R1.4\n93\t      - R2.1\n94\t      - R2.2\n95\t      - R2.3\n96\t      - R2.4\n97\t      - R3.1\n98\t      - R3.2\n99\t      - R3.3\n100\t      - R3.4\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35afd508-ec89-42dc-b408-e4f7fabc1198","uuid":"e1ed2eff-3c39-4e77-81b1-5b02f9c6dfe9","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:14:50.100Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5524/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd081-basenc.yaml","content":"id: srd081-basenc\ntitle: \"cmd/basenc: Encode and Decode with Multiple Alphabets\"\n\nproblem: |\n  GNU basenc is a generalized encoding utility that supports multiple encoding schemes\n  beyond base32 and base64. macOS does not ship basenc. The Go implementation must match\n  the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gbasenc, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n  all flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Encode or decode data using a selectable encoding scheme.\n  - G2: Support Base64, Base64URL, Base32, Base32hex, Base16, and Z85 encodings.\n  - G3: Support line wrapping and garbage ignoring like base32/base64.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gbasenc via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Encoding schemes\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"--base64 must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base64 (same as base64 utility).\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"--base64url must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base64 with URL-safe alphabet (+ and / replaced by - and _).\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"--base32 must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base32 (same as base32 utility).\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"--base32hex must encode/decode using RFC 4648 Base32 with extended hex alphabet.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Additional encodings and options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"--base16 must encode/decode using hexadecimal (Base16). Output is uppercase hex characters.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"--z85 must encode/decode using ZeroMQ Z85 encoding. Input length must be a multiple of 4 bytes for encoding.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-d or --decode must decode the input using the selected encoding scheme.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-w COLS or --wrap=COLS must set the wrap column (default 76). -w 0 disables wrapping.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Input handling and error cases\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-i or --ignore-garbage must ignore non-alphabet characters during decoding.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given).\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 when no encoding scheme is specified, when the file cannot be opened, or when decode input is invalid.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/basenc does not implement Base2 (binary) encoding.\n  - cmd/basenc does not implement custom alphabet specification.\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"echo hello | basenc --base64 produces Base64 encoded output matching gbasenc --base64.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"echo hello | basenc --base16 produces hex output matching gbasenc --base16.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"basenc --base64url encodes with URL-safe alphabet, matching gbasenc --base64url.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gbasenc passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/basenc compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}}}
