{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) submitted stitch task #5524 to implement error handling and multi-file support for `cmd/basenc` (srd081-basenc R3.1-R3.4). The specific requirements are:\n   - R1: Handle invalid input during decoding with appropriate error messages and exit code (SRD R3.1)\n   - R2: Support reading from file arguments in addition to stdin (SRD R3.2)\n   - R3: Handle multiple file arguments by concatenating input (SRD R3.3)\n   - R4: Treat \"-\" as stdin in the file argument list (SRD R3.4)\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/basenc/main.go` and `cmd/basenc/basenc_test.go`. Design decisions require using `pkg/encutil.OpenInput` for file/stdin selection and matching `gbasenc` behavior.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs Homebrew `gbasenc` reference binary\n   - `pkg/encutil.OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)` for file/stdin abstraction\n   - `pkg/encutil.Encode` and `pkg/encutil.Decode` for encoding/decoding operations\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for differential test execution\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Multi-file input concatenation (reading multiple files sequentially as one stream)\n   - Z85, Base64, Base64URL, Base32, Base32hex, Base16 encoding schemes\n   - Go `io.MultiReader` pattern for concatenating multiple readers\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd081-basenc.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements R3.1-R3.4\n     - R3.1: `-i`/`--ignore-garbage` ignores non-alphabet chars during decoding\n     - R3.2: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given)\n     - R3.3: Must exit 1 for missing encoding, unopenable file, or invalid decode input\n     - R3.4: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n     \n   - **cmd/basenc/main.go** (existing, 279 lines)\n     - Already implements: SIGPIPE handler, single file support via `encutil.OpenInput`, `--ignore-garbage` flag, basic error handling (missing encoding, invalid decode)\n     - `parseArgs` returns `(options, string)` - single file only\n     - `main()` opens single file via `encutil.OpenInput(file)`, then calls `encutil.Encode` or `encutil.Decode`\n     - Key gap: No multi-file support. `parseArgs` collects only one file argument. Need to change to return `[]string` and iterate/concatenate inputs.\n     - Key structures: `type options struct { encoding string; decode bool; ignoreGarbage bool; wrap int }`\n     - Full existing main function:\n       ```go\n       func main() {\n           sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n           opts, file := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n           if opts.encoding == \"\" {\n               fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"basenc: missing encoding type\\n\")\n               os.Exit(1)\n           }\n           rc, err := encutil.OpenInput(file)\n           if err != nil {\n               fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"basenc: %s: %s\\n\", file, err.Error())\n               os.Exit(1)\n           }\n           defer rc.Close()\n           if opts.decode {\n               err = encutil.Decode(rc, os.Stdout, encutil.DecoderConfig{...})\n           } else {\n               err = encutil.Encode(rc, os.Stdout, encutil.EncoderConfig{...})\n           }\n           // error handling...\n       }\n       ```\n     \n   - **cmd/basenc/basenc_test.go** (existing, 125 lines)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gbasenc\")`\n     - Has tests for: all encoding schemes (encode/decode), wrap options, ignore-garbage, single file input, stdin, \"-\" as stdin, empty file, missing file, no encoding error, invalid decode error\n     - Missing: multi-file concatenation tests, \"-\" interspersed in multi-file list\n     - Helper: `writeFile(t, path, content)` already exists\n     - Uses `discardStderr` normalizer for error tests: `testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })`\n\n   - **pkg/encutil** (from package_contracts, not read from disk)\n     - `OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)` - returns reader for file or stdin when filename is \"\" or \"-\"\n     - `Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error`\n     - `Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the main gap is multi-file support: `parseArgs` currently returns a single file string. It needs to return `[]string` to support multiple file arguments.\n   - For multi-file concatenation, the approach should be: collect all file args in parseArgs, then in main, open each file via `encutil.OpenInput` and use `io.MultiReader` to concatenate them (or iterate and read sequentially).\n   - Need to handle \"-\" appearing anywhere in the file list as stdin.\n   - When no files are specified, default to reading stdin (same as current behavior).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The entire stitch task #5524 description with project context, requirements, constraints, acceptance criteria, and the instruction to implement cmd/basenc error handling and multi-file support (srd081-basenc R3.1-R3.4).\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/basenc/main.go` to:\n     - Change `parseArgs` to return `[]string` (slice of files) instead of single `string`\n     - Update `main()` to iterate over multiple files, concatenating their input\n     - Handle \"-\" as stdin in the file argument list\n     - Ensure error messages match `gbasenc` format\n   - Modify `cmd/basenc/basenc_test.go` to:\n     - Add differential tests for multi-file concatenation\n     - Add tests for \"-\" interspersed with files\n     - Ensure all error case tests pass differentially against gbasenc\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/basenc/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/basenc/` to verify no issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/basenc/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three key files (SRD, main.go, test file) and was about to plan and implement the changes. I had stated \"I'll start by reading the SRD for basenc (R3.1-R3.4), the existing source files, and the encutil package to understand what needs to be modified.\" The reads completed successfully with all content captured above. Implementation had not yet begun when the summary was requested.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the changes to `cmd/basenc/main.go` and `cmd/basenc/basenc_test.go`:\n   \n   For main.go:\n   - Change `parseArgs` signature from `func parseArgs(args []string) (options, string)` to `func parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string)` to collect multiple file arguments\n   - Update `main()` to open each file via `encutil.OpenInput`, collect the readers, and use `io.MultiReader` to concatenate them before passing to `encutil.Encode`/`encutil.Decode`\n   - When files slice is empty, default to stdin (pass \"\" to OpenInput)\n   - Properly close all opened file handles\n   \n   For basenc_test.go:\n   - Add tests for multi-file concatenation (e.g., encoding two files whose content should concatenate)\n   - Add test for \"-\" mixed with file arguments\n   - Verify tests pass differentially against gbasenc\n\n   Per the task: \"requirements: R2: support reading from file arguments in addition to stdin, R3: handle multiple file arguments by concatenating input, R4: treat '-' as stdin in the file argument list\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, err