{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fv7SiFKPRAfJ3p2EskazmV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the code and test file, I can now provide you with a comprehensive status report on the R3.x requirements for srd081-basenc.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirements.yaml file I found at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5524/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd081-basenc.yaml` contains the specification for the basenc utility, but it doesn't have explicit \"in_progress\" vs \"done\" status markings embedded in the YAML itself.\n\nHowever, by examining the actual implementation in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5524/cmd/basenc/`, I can infer the implementation status:\n\n## R3.x Requirements Status\n\n**R3.1: -i or --ignore-garbage must ignore non-alphabet characters during decoding**\n- Status: **DONE**\n- Implementation: Lines 245-249 in main.go handle the `-i` flag; lines 205-207 handle `--ignore-garbage`; the ignoreGarbage option is passed to `encutil.Decode()` (lines 66-70)\n- Tests: Lines 71-73 in basenc_test.go verify this with multiple encodings\n\n**R3.2: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given)**\n- Status: **DONE**\n- Implementation: Lines 59-64 in main.go use `encutil.OpenInput()` to handle file or stdin; parseArgs() (lines 162-186) correctly parses both file arguments and \"-\" (stdin)\n- Tests: Lines 75-78 in basenc_test.go test file input, empty files, explicit stdin (\"-\"), and implicit stdin\n\n**R3.3: Must exit 1 when no encoding scheme is specified, when file cannot be opened, or when decode input is invalid**\n- Status: **DONE**\n- Implementation: \n  - No encoding (lines 54-57): exits with code 1\n  - File cannot be opened (lines 59-62): exits with code 1\n  - Invalid decode input (lines 77-82): handles via error from `encutil.Decode()`\n- Tests: Lines 80-83 